1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,175
This is VOID.

2
00:00:01,225 --> 00:00:06,570
Give an AI agent real on-chain power, with a guarantee it can never leave your rules.

3
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,918
A smart contract checks every action.

4
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:14,582
Every action passes five gates, in a fixed order.

5
00:00:14,633 --> 00:00:18,761
Expiry, spend cap, whitelist, transaction count, rate limit.

6
00:00:18,811 --> 00:00:20,920
Illegal actions stop at a gate.

7
00:00:21,270 --> 00:00:22,508
Let's build a vault.

8
00:00:22,558 --> 00:00:29,012
I set the owner, and the one contract and function the agent may call, then seal the policy on-chain.

9
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:30,429
Live, on Base Sepolia.

10
00:00:33,058 --> 00:00:33,588
Sealed.

11
00:00:33,638 --> 00:00:34,998
Five gates armed.

12
00:00:35,048 --> 00:00:39,144
I fund it with test ETH, and take the session key.

13
00:00:39,194 --> 00:00:41,217
Shown once, never stored.

14
00:00:41,567 --> 00:00:42,953
Now I am the agent.

15
00:00:43,003 --> 00:00:45,599
I try something outside the policy.

16
00:00:45,649 --> 00:00:46,355
Simulated:

17
00:00:46,405 --> 00:00:48,246
blocked at the whitelist.

18
00:00:48,296 --> 00:00:49,228
Now for real.

19
00:00:50,361 --> 00:00:51,504
Reverted on-chain.

20
00:00:51,554 --> 00:00:54,552
The chain itself refused it, not an app check.

21
00:00:55,792 --> 00:00:58,417
Same key, doing what the policy allows.

22
00:00:58,467 --> 00:01:00,131
It goes straight through.

23
00:01:00,181 --> 00:01:01,571
No human in the loop.

24
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:11,736
If anything looks wrong, one owner signature pulls the plug.

25
00:01:17,506 --> 00:01:19,920
Now every action is blocked at the first gate.

26
00:01:22,168 --> 00:01:24,640
And what is left sweeps straight back to the owner.

27
00:01:27,218 --> 00:01:28,147
One more test.

28
00:01:28,197 --> 00:01:28,986
That was me.

29
00:01:29,036 --> 00:01:33,462
So I told a real AI agent it was hijacked, and to drain a vault.

30
00:01:33,512 --> 00:01:40,386
It tried the whole balance, sneaking under the cap, a token transfer, even uninstalling the policy.

31
00:01:40,436 --> 00:01:42,554
Five attempts, five rejections.

32
00:01:42,604 --> 00:01:45,142
The one approved action went through.

33
00:01:48,347 --> 00:01:53,572
Real ERC-4337, twenty-eight Foundry tests, live on Base and Arbitrum.

34
00:01:53,622 --> 00:01:53,954
VOID:

35
00:01:54,004 --> 00:01:58,388
session keys for agents that the contract itself enforces.
